{"duration_api_ms":1813651,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"8ab6682a-3eba-4ac5-96e7-fb459630bd7b","total_cost_usd":53.84577000000002,"usage":{"input_tokens":24,"cache_creation_input_tokens":51264,"cache_read_input_tokens":7917283,"output_tokens":19882,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":5679},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":51264,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3358,"cache_read_input_tokens":678012,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3749,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3749},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5[1m]":{"inputTokens":436,"outputTokens":184617,"thinkingTokens":58269,"cacheReadInputTokens":84821110,"cacheCreationInputTokens":681761,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":53.84577000000002,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":14,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"All three codex complaints were valid, and all three are fixed in the working tree. `dart analyze lib test` exits 0 and `flutter test` passes 53/53, including 3 new tests for joining MP4 segments.\n\n**R3 — multi-segment MP4 is now joined into one mp4.** There is a new progressive-MP4 reader (`lib/utils/mp4_join.dart`, another `part` of `mp4_remux.dart`) that feeds the same writer the FLV path uses.\n- It reads every sample from each segment's sample tables: sizes, durations, composition offsets, sync flags, chunk layout and chunk offsets (`stsz`/`stz2`, `stts`, `ctts`, `stss`, `stsc`, `stco`/`co64`). Sample bytes are copied unchanged.\n- Each segment starts where the longest track of the previous segment ended; the gap is added to the other tracks' last sample so audio and video stay in sync.\n- The first segment's edit list is kept, but its playing edit is extended to the end of the joined track.\n- All segments must have the same tracks and byte-identical `stsd` and timescale. Otherwise, or if a segment is fragmented, it throws `UnsupportedError`. `_exportType1` then falls back to the current behaviour: separate files `<base>.mp4`, `<base>.2.mp4`, …\n- A single mp4 segment is still moved as is. Exposed as `Mp4Remuxer.joinMp4`.\n\n**R4 — image saving failed.** `CommentImages.save()` now creates the `comments_images/` folder before downloading into it.\n\n**R6 — iOS product name was still Runner.**\n- `PRODUCT_NAME` is `LibrePili` in all three Runner build configs.\n- The product file reference and the scheme's `BuildableName` are `LibrePili.app`.\n- The iOS CI now uses `Payload/LibrePili.app` for codesign and zip. `Payload` links to `build/ios/iphoneos`, where Flutter writes `<PRODUCT_NAME>.app`. There is no iOS test target, so nothing else refers to `Runner.app`.\n\n## Diff (files touched in this refinement)\n\nNew file, not in `git diff`:\n- `lib/utils/mp4_join.dart` — 296 lines.\n\nTest file (gitignored, needs force-adding):\n- `test/utils/flv_demux_test.dart` — added a `joinMp4` test group and an `_indexOf` helper, now 369 lines. The tests cover reading a progressive mp4 back sample for sample, joining two segments in timeline order (with an order check), and refusing to join segments with a different codec configuration.\n\n```diff\n--- a/lib/services/download/download_extras.dart   (CommentImages.save)\n       if (!file.existsSync()) {\n+        await file.parent.create(recursive: true);\n         final part = '${file.path}.part';\n\n--- a/lib/services/download/download_service.dart  (_exportType1)\n-  /// Old single-URL (durl) streams. FLV with H.264 + AAC is remuxed into a\n-  /// real mp4, all segments joined; a single mp4 segment is moved as is.\n-  /// Anything else keeps its own data and extension (several segments:\n-  /// `<base>.flv`, `<base>.2.flv`, ...). Returns the (first) exported file.\n+  /// Old single-URL (durl) streams. FLV with H.264 + AAC is remuxed into a\n+  /// real mp4 and MP4 segments are joined, all segments in timeline order; a\n+  /// single mp4 segment is moved as is. When that is not possible (other\n+  /// codecs, segments with differing codec configuration) the original data\n+  /// is kept with its own extension (several segments: `<base>.flv`,\n+  /// `<base>.2.flv`, ...). Returns the (first) exported file.\n   static Future<String> _exportType1(List<String> inputs, String output) async {\n     final isFlv = Mp4Remuxer.isFlv(inputs.first);\n-    if (isFlv) {\n+    if (!isFlv && inputs.length == 1) {\n+      await _moveFile(inputs.first, output);\n+      return output;\n+    }\n+    if (isFlv || inputs.every(Mp4Remuxer.isMp4)) {\n       try {\n         await Isolate.run(\n-          () => Mp4Remuxer.remuxFlv(inputs: inputs, output: output),\n+          () => isFlv\n+              ? Mp4Remuxer.remuxFlv(inputs: inputs, output: output)\n+              : Mp4Remuxer.joinMp4(inputs: inputs, output: output),\n         );\n         return output;\n       } on UnsupportedError catch (e) {\n-        if (kDebugMode) debugPrint('FLV kept as is: $e');\n+        if (kDebugMode) debugPrint('segments kept as they are: $e');\n       }\n-    } else if (inputs.length == 1) {\n-      await _moveFile(inputs.first, output);\n-      return output;\n     }\n\n--- a/lib/utils/mp4_remux.dart   (additions relative to the previous turn)\n part 'flv_demux.dart';\n+part 'mp4_join.dart';\n ...\n+  /// Joins progressive MP4 segments (in timeline order) into one MP4.\n+  /// Throws [UnsupportedError] when the segments' tracks or codec\n+  /// configurations differ, so the caller can keep them separate.\n+  static Future<void> joinMp4({\n+    required List<String> inputs,\n+    required String output,\n+    void Function(int copied, int total)? onProgress,\n+  }) async {\n+    if (inputs.isEmpty) throw ArgumentError('no input');\n+    await _write(_Mp4Joiner.join(inputs), output, onProgress);\n+  }\n+\n   /// The tracks an FLV demux produces; for tests only.\n-  static List<Map<String, Object>> debugFlvTracks(List<String> inputs) => [\n-    for (final t in _FlvDemuxer.demux(inputs))\n+  static List<Map<String, Object>> debugFlvTracks(List<String> inputs) =>\n+      _debugSummary(_FlvDemuxer.demux(inputs));\n+\n+  /// The tracks [joinMp4] reads from progressive MP4 inputs; for tests only.\n+  static List<Map<String, Object>> debugMp4JoinTracks(List<String> inputs) =>\n+      _debugSummary(_Mp4Joiner.join(inputs));\n+\n+  static List<Map<String, Object>> _debugSummary(List<_Track> tracks) => [\n+    for (final t in tracks)\n       { ...same map as before... },\n   ];\n\n--- a/ios/Runner.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj\n-\t\t97C146EE1CF9000F007C117D /* Runner.app */ = {... path = Runner.app; ...};\n+\t\t97C146EE1CF9000F007C117D /* LibrePili.app */ = {... path = LibrePili.app; ...};\n-\t\t\t\t97C146EE1CF9000F007C117D /* Runner.app */,\n+\t\t\t\t97C146EE1CF9000F007C117D /* LibrePili.app */,\n-\t\t\tproductReference = 97C146EE1CF9000F007C117D /* Runner.app */;\n+\t\t\tproductReference = 97C146EE1CF9000F007C117D /* LibrePili.app */;\n-\t\t\t\tPRODUCT_NAME = \"$(TARGET_NAME)\";      (x3, Runner Debug/Release/Profile)\n+\t\t\t\tPRODUCT_NAME = LibrePili;\n\n--- a/ios/Runner.xcodeproj/xcshareddata/xcschemes/Runner.xcscheme\n-               BuildableName = \"Runner.app\"          (x4)\n+               BuildableName = \"LibrePili.app\"\n\n--- a/.github/workflows/ios.yml\n-          find Payload/Runner.app/Frameworks -type d -name \"*.framework\" -exec codesign ...\n-          zip -r9 LibrePili_ios_${{env.version}}.ipa Payload/Runner.app\n+          find Payload/LibrePili.app/Frameworks -type d -name \"*.framework\" -exec codesign ...\n+          zip -r9 LibrePili_ios_${{env.version}}.ipa Payload/LibrePili.app\n```\n\n## Uncertainty\n\n- **R3:**\n  - The tests use segments made by our own writer, so they don't exercise `stz2`, `co64` or several samples per chunk.\n  - Edit lists from segments after the first are dropped; each segment is assumed to start at media time 0.\n  - Segments whose tracks come in a different order would be refused as a configuration mismatch, not reordered.\n- **R6:**\n  - Not built. I'm relying on Flutter writing `build/ios/iphoneos/<PRODUCT_NAME>.app`.\n  - The Xcode target is still named `Runner`, as Flutter requires, so `Podfile` and the scheme name are unchanged.\n\n```\nTEST RESULTS:\n  runner: dart analyze + flutter test\n  command: source \".../local_env.sh\" && cd \"$REPO\" && dart analyze lib test && flutter test\n  exit_code: 0\n  total: 53\n  passed: 53\n  failed: 0\n  skipped: 0\n  duration_ms: 36000\n\nINFRA REPAIRS (during auto-repair, empty if none):\n\nREAL FAILURES (audit-fix-caused regressions, empty if none):\n\nINFRA-PERSISTENT (failures that hit the 3-cycle repair cap, empty if none):\n\nOVERALL: PASS\n```\n\n`dart analyze` reports 36 infos, the same count as before; none are in the files I touched.\n\nMCP note: Gmail, Google Calendar and Google Drive still need authorizing in claude.ai connector settings, and agentbridge failed to connect. Neither was needed here.","ttft_ms":6276,"type":"result","duration_ms":405102,"uuid":"bda6726f-a6bb-4fb3-a445-4afd96701b5f","ttft_stream_ms":3284,"time_to_request_ms":781,"first_content_frame_ms":3284,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
